<!--
  Agent mark — a square head with a prompt on its face.

  A terminal window, then a ghost, then this. Both earlier marks failed for the
  same reason: they described a *thing* rather than a *face*. A mascot is
  decorative; a head with a prompt in it is the machine's expression, and it is
  the one image that says both "this is an agent" and "it is looking at a shell"
  without a label.

  Drawn on a 24x24 viewport that it fills, so a 19dp call site shows a 19dp mark.
  The first mark needed a 2048 viewport and a group transform to rescale artwork
  occupying 46% of its canvas — the empty viewport, not the icon size, had been
  the problem, and it took a three-paragraph comment to explain.

  Solid head with the prompt cut as holes (evenOdd) rather than painted in a
  second colour: Icon() applies one ColorFilter over the whole drawable, so a
  two-tone path collapses to flat colour the moment it is tinted and the prompt
  disappears into the face. A hole cannot be filled by a tint.

  The corner radius is 2.1 units — enough to stop the corners reading as a
  rendering error, small enough that the silhouette stays square. A larger
  radius turns it into a rounded square, which reads as an app icon rather than
  a head.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">

    <!-- Head: rounded square, plus two holes for "> _" -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M5.4,2.6
            L18.6,2.6
            C19.82,2.6 20.8,3.58 20.8,4.8
            L20.8,19.2
            C20.8,20.42 19.82,21.4 18.6,21.4
            L5.4,21.4
            C4.18,21.4 3.2,20.42 3.2,19.2
            L3.2,4.8
            C3.2,3.58 4.18,2.6 5.4,2.6
            Z
            M8.5,8.9
            L12,12
            L8.5,15.1
            L7.1,13.8
            L9.4,12
            L7.1,10.2
            Z
            M12.9,13.4
            L16.4,13.4
            L16.4,14.8
            L12.9,14.8
            Z" />
</vector>
